{"id": "EUVD-2026-108907", "enisaUuid": "60d02da8-ac33-38d3-8e43-8c1341d9d5ec", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtc: dev: zero-initialize struct rtc_wkalrm to prevent information leak\n\nThe struct rtc_wkalrm has padding holes after the 'pending' member.\nWhen returned to userspace via the RTC_WKALRM_RD ioctl, uninitialized\nkernel stack data residing in these holes may be leaked.\n\nZero-initialize the struct at declaration to eliminate this information\nleak risk.\n\nFixes smatch warnings:\n- drivers/rtc/dev.c:392 rtc_dev_ioctl() warn: check that 'alarm' doesn't\n  leak information (struct has a hole after 'pending')", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:11:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:11:46", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2215eb3cbbd3d9d73cc18c08e3ef53f903443cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/beda3c9730ad3087d01aa1d0415c40942042ec87", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00dc50cede96738dadc64b20e671186cddb8a58d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2838d7bbb551861c25187dfb581ed6e7a56762e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ee5c5d804d592a8328a425b9274487d393d3a05"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98935"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1289158f-db1c-359c-aca7-86a0817b470a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "2ebe2a8e-af69-3ed9-9a45-57ba40d83c19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "36e14f5fdfdf7cec8887b7ff69cd9bb5051ecf62 <2838d7bbb551861c25187dfb581ed6e7a56762e9"}, {"id": "3c0355ca-b8ab-3d5d-b2a9-09bcf9c415c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "36e14f5fdfdf7cec8887b7ff69cd9bb5051ecf62 <0ee5c5d804d592a8328a425b9274487d393d3a05"}, {"id": "407822e0-1c13-3c2c-95bb-1c494e1c683d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "67c83403-0287-34fa-8a98-6cd